<title>GERMANY: Depfa extends gains, trades up 11.8 pct.</title>
<headline>Depfa extends gains, trades up 11.8 pct.</headline>
<dateline>FRANKFURT 1997-03-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in German mortgage bank DePfa Bank AG extended their gains to trade up 11.8 percent at 90 marks in pre-bourse electronic trade, after the bank said it understood Switzerland's UBS had bought a stake in it.</p>
<p>The bank said a shareholder study had shown UBS held approximately nine percent of its stock, and said it had not held any co-operation talks with the Swiss bank.</p>
<p>A statement released by DePfa earlier included a denial by UBS of any knowledge of such a stake held by it in DePfa.</p>
<p>The 30-share DAX index was up 1.3 percent at 3,470.70 points.</p>
<p>--Frankfurt Newsroom, +49 69 756525</p>
</text>
